---
pagination:
  data: redirects
  size: 1
  alias: r
permalink: "{{ r.from }}/index.html"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Redirect stubs for the old site's URLs (data/redirects.json, resolved in lib/load-data.js).
    GitHub Pages has no server redirects, so each old path gets a tiny page: meta refresh and
    location.replace to the target (both with the path prefix via the url filter), a visible
    link, canonical to the target on the real domain, noindex. Excluded from collections, so it is
    never in the sitemap or navigation; scripts/check-redirects.mjs verifies every target. -#}
{%- set target = r.to | url -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>This page has moved | {{ site.name }}</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ r.to | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ target }}">
<script>location.replace({{ target | dump | safe }});</script>
</head>
<body>
<p>This page has moved. <a href="{{ target }}">Continue to the new page</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
